## 📂 Project Directory Structure

The project has been organized into modular components targeting various customer, operational, and admin touchpoints:

*   **`ResortApp/`**: Core FastAPI Python backend repository.
    *   `app/api/`: Modular routing layers defining REST API endpoints (40+ operational domains).
    *   `app/models/`: SQLAlchemy DB models detailing system objects (Rooms, Bookings, Expenses, JEs, Inventory).
    *   `app/schemas/`: Pydantic validation schemas.
    *   `app/core/`: Security configurations, JWT handling, and request-response middlewares.
    *   `app/utils/`: Auxiliary engines (caching, accounting helpers, PDF generation).
*   **`dasboard/`**: Admin/Management Dashboard frontend codebase.
    *   React app using **Tailwind CSS**. Serves managers and financial admins.
    *   Consists of heavyweight screens (`Inventory.jsx` ~482KB, `Bookings.jsx` ~361KB, `Services.jsx` ~361KB) indicating extensive business rules handled on the client side.
*   **`userend/`**: Guest Booking and In-house customer portal.
    *   React app using **Tailwind CSS**. Facilitates room reservations, activity selection, service requests, and food ordering.
    *   Consolidates core flows into `App.js` (~378KB).
*   **`Mobile/`**: Flutter repository containing cross-platform Android/iOS codebases:
    *   `employee/`: Operational flow for room service, housekeeping updates, and restaurant table allocations.
    *   `owner/`: Executive dashboard rendering high-level charts, occupancy graphs, and day-audit KPIs.
    *   `orchid_employee_app.apk` & `zeebull_owner_app.apk`: Precompiled production binary logs.
*   **`landingpage/`**: Marketing website.
    *   Clean static assets (HTML5, Vanilla CSS, JS) mounted directly onto the FastAPI entrypoint under the `/` path to maximize SEO ranking and page speed.

